# Kello01b input route (UU/seconds): first route by player input.
# The PlayerStart is on the snow mountain's north flank (rotation yaw 3496 = 19.2 deg ENE);
# the level's own facing is the descent. Hold that facing east along y~4700-4900, then turn
# south at x~-2.7k and drop the east face of the massif to the chalet snow field (z~2075).
# No teleports, grants, goal writes or control overrides.
#
# The chalet's north wall (K_chalet03) blocks a straight approach; the front door Porte0
# (XIDCine.Porte, XIIIPorte.PlayerTriggerToggle, KeyNum 0) opens through its own
# PlayerTrigger (the Grab key) and then swings its leaf ~96 deg. Walking straight south into
# the opening wedges the player on the swung leaf, so the route retreats north, re-approaches
# the doorway from the west of the hinge, and enters; TouchTrigger2 (Event='XIII_dans_chalet')
# then fires the Cine0 cutscene (CineController21 -> PlayingSequence).
#
# item99d: the whole cutscene now runs (the flashback `wait warning` is released by the
# DialogueManager line-end warning once references to the map's pending-kill `Cine2` speaker are
# nulled at load). Cine0/Cine1 reach `destroy self` at ~226 s and `event objectif99` promotes
# goal 0 to primary.
#
# item99e: the post-cutscene firefight is survived by input, not by the chalet shotgun. The
# `FusilPompePick0`/`MiniUziPick0`/`MagnumPick0` weapons sit on a lower floor (z~1930) below the
# fully-enclosed goal-trigger room floor (z~2091) and are unreachable; the item99d route fought
# unarmed (`Fists`) and only survived because an AI friendly-fire rocket happened to kill the
# close shotgun soldier `BaseSoldier2`. The route now grabs the reachable west-floor `M60Pick1`
# through the game's own interaction Grab (`track M60Pick1` + `use`), selects it with the retail
# `next_weapon` key, returns to the wardrobe cover and kills the close `BaseSoldier2`, then
# crosses the map's own goal triggers (`XIIIGoalTrigger2`->goal 0, `XIIIGoalTrigger1`->goal 1).
# Goal 0 completes only when the level's own `objectif0` event fires, so goal 0/1 and the
# PRock01a travel stay unreached by this route.
